       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. The maximum for ibuprofen in adults is 3,200 mg/day, so this is twice the limit.\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is also twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Risks at this level:** The main risks are GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Her normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove them.\n\n**Possible intended orders**\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO three or four times daily (2,400\u20133,200 mg/day), for example for inflammatory pain or arthritis.\n- Ibuprofen 400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours as needed for routine analgesia.\n- 1600 mg may have been meant as the total daily dose, which would be 400 mg four times daily.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give a clinical rationale. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy before it's entered."
      }
     ],
